<h2>Lactose Intolerance and the DQ Non-Dairy Dilly Bar</h2>
<p>Approximately 36% of Americans experience some degree of lactose intolerance. For guests in this group, most of the <a href="/">Dairy Queen Menu</a> is off-limits — Blizzards, soft serve cones, sundaes, and shakes all contain significant dairy. The Non-Dairy Dilly Bar is the one exception in the frozen novelty category. At $2.49, it is a genuine dairy-free treat that fits naturally into the DQ experience rather than feeling like a compromise.</p>
<h2>Non-Dairy vs. Dairy-Free — What the Distinction Means</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Non-Dairy</strong> means the product formula does not include dairy ingredients like milk, cream, or butter.</li>
<li><strong>Dairy-Free</strong> is a broader claim that also covers cross-contamination from shared equipment and facilities.</li>
<li>The DQ Non-Dairy Dilly Bar qualifies as non-dairy by formulation. For strict dairy-free requirements (severe allergy or celiac-level sensitivity), verify cross-contamination practices with your specific location.</li>
</ul>
